# kk: Avoid kernel panic due to out of device memory in Metal
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46368 state=merged
# ### What does this MR do and why?
<!-- Describe in detail what your merge request does and why. -->

The first iteration of https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-ValidationLayers/pull/13708 crashed the CI machine that led to this issue. Only present in macOS 26

```
kk: Avoid kernel panic due to out of device memory in Metal

Metal doesn't handle correctly out of device memory resulting in a kernel
panic. Limit allocations to 95% of suggested maximum memory usage by Metal.

Signed-off-by: Aitor Camacho <aitor@lunarg.com>
```
--- docs/drivers/kosmickrisp/workarounds.rst
